Linux before 6.14 (064737920bdb "arm64: Filter out SVE hwcaps when FEAT_SVE isn't
implemented", also in 6.13.3, 6.12.14 and 6.6.79) sets HWCAP2_SVE2 from
ID_AA64ZFR0_EL1 alone, so it can be set while HWCAP_SVE is clear: in a VM on an
Apple M4, which has SME and no SVE, for one. Highway took HWCAP2_SVE2 alone as
SVE2 and then read the vector length with `cntb`, which is SIGILL there.

--- a/hwy/targets.cc
+++ b/hwy/targets.cc
@@ -535,7 +535,7 @@
 
   constexpr CapBits kGroupSVE2 = HWCAP2_SVE2 | HWCAP2_SVEAES;
   const CapBits hw2 = getauxval(AT_HWCAP2);
-  if ((hw2 & kGroupSVE2) == kGroupSVE2) {
+  if ((hw2 & kGroupSVE2) == kGroupSVE2 && (bits & HWY_SVE)) {
     bits |= HWY_SVE2;
   }
 
